<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="GE 101" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2006" href="schedule/2006.xml">2006</calendarYear><term id="120061" href="schedule/2006/spring.xml">Spring 2006</term><subject id="GE" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE.xml">General Engineering</subject></parents><label>Engineering Graphics &amp; Design</label><description>Use of computer-aided design (CAD) software to model parts and assemblies. Use of parametric and non-parametric solids, surface and wireframe models. Part editing, two-dimensional documentation of models. Planar projection theory, including sketching of perspective, isometric, multiview, auxiliary, and section views. Spatial visualization exercises. Dimensioning guidelines, tolerancing techniques. Team design project. </description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sections><section id="33058" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33058.xml">ABA</section><section id="33063" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33063.xml">ABC</section><section id="33066" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33066.xml">ABE</section><section id="33068" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33068.xml">AL1</section><section id="33070" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33070.xml">BBA</section><section id="33072" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33072.xml">BBB</section><section id="33074" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33074.xml">BBC</section><section id="33077" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33077.xml">BBD</section><section id="33085" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33085.xml">BBG</section><section id="33086" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33086.xml">BBH</section><section id="33091" href="schedule/2006/spring/GE/101/33091.xml">BL1</section></sections></ns2:course>